<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU releases €6.6 billion for members arming Ukraine as seven killed in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdc90518baefa80a81c006cd37af0c1276a32be24b901bb129a1577c46c45b82</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T17:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-_6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv--228cd20fb306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-%E2%82%AC6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">European Union countries have agreed to release €6.6 billion from a fund meant to reimburse member states that have  provided arms to Ukraine, EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said on Friday. At least seven people were killed in Russian strikes on Kyiv earlier in the day, according to local authorities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU vows to pursue €120 million fine on X after US backs Musk's court challenge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fe84ce40739efb3ff4ebf712c2eb33402b1533cbebb4d46e7a2b90e483437b1</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:01:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-_120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge--67ad47c60d3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-%E2%82%AC120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Friday said it will pursue a €120 million fine against the X social network after the US Justice Department said it supported the efforts of X owner Elon Musk to have the case annulled. The bloc fined the platform in 2025 for breaching EU online transparency rules, notably with its pay-to-play blue "verification" checkmark.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Moldova is the best performer in my class': EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a7071ca8d1e86a50c5ddf4ef8cc3382fbc05e0a8ee5414085401c3cb61ceb9a</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:54:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos--14965558a28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos" /><summary type="html">The EU has gone through seven waves of enlargement since 1973, but there has not been one since Croatia joined in 2013. Indeed, there are not likely to be any new members in the club before 2028 – some 15 years after Croatia entered. But 2026 undeniably has momentum, and is on track to be a record year in terms of opening and closing new chapters for existing applicants. That is why our guest, EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos, sees this as "the year of the enlargement."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Climate breakdown: Is the EU adapting to the new normal? Europe's summer of disasters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91bf682ffe2278db6c84222bec8385b7b4f0508b18a73510b80071d76a9e3783</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters--f8e97073c504.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters" /><summary type="html">It has been called Europe's disaster year. 2026 has seen more than 30,000 excess deaths linked to heatwaves, along with mega wildfires, nuclear power plants having to shut down, gas plants under pressure, droughts reducing hydropower generation from rivers and wild fluctuations in electricity prices, not to mention major disruptions to crops and farming in general.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump made ‘final decision’ to allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36ae867cf1701c81572965bccf4547d18e06edffb5bd2a9cea6fe1f34a092c98</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:46:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-trump-made-final-decision-to-give-ukraine-patriot-licence-zelensky-says--92e787840dd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-trump-made-final-decision-to-give-ukraine-patriot-licence-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump told President Volodymyr Zelensky that he had made a "final decision" to grant Kyiv the licence to produce Patriot air defence missiles, the Ukrainian leader said Friday. The assurance came during the last meeting between the two leaders, Zelensky said, capping a period of uncertainty after a series of reversals on the issue.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>From 'Jungle' to jungles, migrants in Calais continue to dream of UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08f2d2aa16e4542e57c528f8005b86fdd230bf1e692cedaae25c8bf94452df9e</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:30:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk--93cc7b8e4722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk" /><summary type="html">October 2026 marks 10 years since the Calais "Jungle" in northern France was dismantled by French police. The camp was home to thousands of migrants who wanted to cross the Channel and reach the UK. A decade on, migrants continue to dream of reaching British shores and the "Jungle" has been replaced by many smaller jungles scattered along the northern French coastline. FRANCE 24's Pauline Godart, Claire Paccalin and Mohamed Farhat report.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV’s visit to France: What you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:298013035eaeca47c22febd8dc09d4aceef4018b7774eef3fd5801942fdec85e</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T07:50:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-s-visit-to-france-what-you-need-to-know--963416a8ae42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-s-visit-to-france-what-you-need-to-know" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Friday arrives in France for a four-day visit – his fifth Apostolic journey since becoming pontiff last year – during which he hopes to repair the Catholic Church’s standing after sexual abuse scandals while also addressing issues such as the need to regulate AI. FRANCE 24 guides you through his visit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Most powerful force is human potential': Ukraine's military prioritises new tactics, technologies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc165b04cb8167684705c93afb4f4e4ba5907de645808bf5d3d95b29b6aefaec</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T07:11:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260925-our-most-powerful-force-is-human-potential-ukraine-military-prioritises-new-tactics-technol--bb5590fdf2b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260925-our-most-powerful-force-is-human-potential-ukraine-military-prioritises-new-tactics-technologies" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Kyrylo Berkal, Deputy Commander of Ukraine's Third Army Corps. He sees Ukraine’s struggle centred on human potential, adaptation and will. While Ukraine is outnumbered, outgunned and sometimes outflanked, their answer is to make human initiative a weapon: giving soldiers and sergeants room to innovate, developing technology from the tactical level upward, and trying to outthink their adversary. Berkal says that Operation Vivaldi embodies that philosophy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo finishes first day of France tour with youth vigil at Paris stadium</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2352e4e912b1c1df50b843b568910247baf8d48755b20aab2530024d01101028</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:57:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years--58e532ec129c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years" /><summary type="html">An estimated 80,000 people welcomed Pope Leo XIV to the Stade de France stadium in Saint-Denis near Paris on Friday. The pontiff warned earlier in the day that an AI "paradise of machines" risked undermining humanity in a speech at the Élysée presidential palace. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Schism with rebel Catholic sect casts a pall over Pope Leo’s visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c04669a105032e293756e014f6bad2e63490f6d31662ce7610f079bdbcab961</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:18:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes--83fe705c42fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes" /><summary type="html">The Vatican’s recent excommunication of followers of a Catholic splinter sect, the Society of Saint Pius X, has revived a longstanding feud within the Roman Catholic Church ahead of Pope Leo XIV’s state visit to France. The ultra-conservative group has established an extensive network of schools and has attracted thousands of followers in France.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU sanctions Russian pundit Xenia Fedorova after expulsion from France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2f0c434039a036f66c6904112f5013f4bf5f918953202a4c3dd9a6cac3eda21</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:45:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france--257744e3539a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Thursday imposed sanctions on Russian commentator Xenia Fedorova, whom France expelled in August over claims that she was disseminating "pro-Russian narratives" in the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>‘Massive, maximum destruction’: Putin seeks to bring Ukrainian civilians ‘to their knees’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60ce5973b3f5e7202933176427d8794d3883bf473c0e34e25bcc4d602f80ff47</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees--80c7cbe71ca4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev from Kyiv, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative. According to Zalmayev, Russia’s ongoing attacks on Ukraine reflect a broader political logic in which military force, political objectives and territorial ambitions are intertwined as instruments of Russian strategy. He argues that Moscow’s attacks on civilian infrastructure are designed to exert extreme pressure on Ukrainian society while demonstrating fierce retaliation to domestic audiences in Russia. Zalmayev contrasts this with Ukraine’s strikes on Russian energy infrastructure, which he describes as targeting assets that directly sustain Moscow’s war effort.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia slams Kyiv with ballistic missiles as Ukrainians brace for harsh winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88ddee564c032afed7aa67d77687f0ff550a6ec5d339100d780a6cca2f138723</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T05:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-as-moscow-steps-up-attacks-kyiv-residents-brace-for-harsh-winter--19e70fb342f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-as-moscow-steps-up-attacks-kyiv-residents-brace-for-harsh-winter" /><summary type="html">Russia on Thursday hit Kyiv with ballistic missiles and drones, killing two people, while a strike on a farm in the Kharkiv region killed six, according to Ukrainian officials. As autumn approaches, Ukrainians are bracing for a tough winter following Moscow's intensifying attacks on the country's energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Ukrainian President Zelensky addresses the UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edf0cca0e599224a2bfef5de93ab4a34d6fd4a49c293ff0e8501dd67076ba64b</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-ukrainian-president-zelensky-addresses-the-un-general-assembly--ac3edf47a818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-ukrainian-president-zelensky-addresses-the-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky urged the world’s leaders Wednesday to keep choking Russia’s revenues and impede its war efforts, telling the UN General Assembly that “Russia’s revenues must remain a target”. Watch his full speech above.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky accuses Putin of using nationals of 47 countries to fight Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0bc65ba3b04ede96d841d017f1b37bba05a36e094df32af311c4f9bd5a2b55b</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:53:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un--ae57344b771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky told the UN General Assembly on Wednesday that Russian President Vladimir Putin had enlisted fighters from 47 countries including North Korea, Ghana and India to fight against Ukraine. Zelensky also warned that his forces could target Russian heating and energy facilities in the winter months if Moscow continues to attack Ukraine's energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe lifts sanctions against two Russians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2a81167b608eaabade3e4f5137960dbc98e237d42ca6fad11656bfbc818bbc6</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:26:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-lifts-sanctions-against-two-russians--469d5d1dff02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-lifts-sanctions-against-two-russians" /><summary type="html">The EU has agreed to remove Russian billionaires Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman from its sanctions list, while extending restrictions on nearly 3,000 individuals and companies linked to Russia’s war in Ukraine for another three years. The decision came after difficult negotiations, as EU sanctions require unanimous approval from all 27 member states. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Azerbaijan pardons jailed Frenchman after EU lifts sanctions on Russian billionaires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e4da4d90ed22d05c65d5e7b60e12b7dd3f69e8c0193d0ff9a2f5c949641e5a</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T07:53:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-azerbaijan-pardons-jailed-frenchman-after-eu-lifts-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs--f2fa9efc0215.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-azerbaijan-pardons-jailed-frenchman-after-eu-lifts-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs" /><summary type="html">Azerbaijan's President ​Ilham Aliyev on Wednesday pardoned a ​French national imprisoned for espionage a day ​after ‌the ⁠EU lifted sanctions on two Russian billionaires.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says Ukraine is ready for an energy ceasefire with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a98c57d5d09408d046732a796a3ddf452a3e033d522fd705cd6157b0a060ed71</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T21:38:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-zelensky-says-ukraine-is-ready-for-an-energy-ceasefire-with-russia--85f40fba8089.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-zelensky-says-ukraine-is-ready-for-an-energy-ceasefire-with-russia" /><summary type="html">On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York on Tuesday, Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky told journalists that Kyiv is ready to halt strikes on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, with hopes to end the war before winter.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Viral NATO video falsely framed as 'war propaganda' against Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a05ccb57fcca76703edf9732961071797bfcc648a3f411f2ad3871bf66acdf62</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T20:44:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1--764414d9cbe1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1" /><summary type="html">A viral NATO video is being falsely framed online as "war propaganda", with users accusing the Alliance of sharing a "promotional video" designed to prepare the public for imminent war with Russia. But the footage is not new: NATO published it in July 2024 for its 75th anniversary, and it's been stripped of its original context. The claim comes as European leaders warn of growing Russian hybrid threats, including alleged drone, cyber and sabotage activity. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>How is the EU responding to record fuel prices?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8bd8c2e823c8239fcdcd9dfbaa43ec9fa549360bbddf2113bdac523c9fd4d96</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices--5f583fca1c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices" /><summary type="html">Fuel prices have hit record highs across Europe in recent days, driven by soaring oil prices amid the war in the Middle East and Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries. However, the scale of the increases, as well as the measures taken to address them, varies significantly from one EU country to another. Here’s why.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ladin: Dolomites villages refuse to give up on ancient language</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96dea56ea071135513a12b9e9ab848c25d4ece7c394832749164f4815135e560</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:30:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language--e899b61b23c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language" /><summary type="html">Year after year, the mountains of the Dolomites become more popular with tourists. Amid millions of visitors, 30,000 inhabitants speak a language only they understand: Ladin, one of the oldest minority languages in Europe.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Greenland agreement 'doesn't really give the US many more rights', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:415ea306dd6f47ebe60188b5ef7668f2dd6e1fb7342de0f90501127ec7887970</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T11:07:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260922-greenland-agreement-doesn-t-really-give-the-us-many-more-rights-expert-says--9bcdd8daa0a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260922-greenland-agreement-doesn-t-really-give-the-us-many-more-rights-expert-says" /><summary type="html">As the US, Denmark and Greenland itself sign an agreement on Greenland's security, we've been asking what difference it will actually make. Our expert says the deal won't really give the US many more rights, but that US President Donald Trump wanted to prevent at all costs the tiny risk of Greenland turning towards China. He adds that for Trump voters, if you inflate the risk, people will talk about it and see you're acting. We spoke in Perspective to Mikaa Blugeon-Mered, Senior Researcher on Hydrogen and Arctic Affairs at the Canada Research Chair in Clean Hydrogen at the University of Québec Trois Rivières.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>First New York, now Berlin: Why the left turn for major metropolises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:174efb0c39924d60f3e18a2ad92c9c2b7907f99ad465cd52b28542c036cc1162</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:56:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-first-new-york-now-berlin-why-the-left-turn-for-major-metropolises--e4e270ca3644.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-first-new-york-now-berlin-why-the-left-turn-for-major-metropolises" /><summary type="html">There's the inroads of the far right, but also the broader desire for change. Introducing Berlin's answer to Zohran Mamdani: Elif Eralp, who led the far-left Die Linke party's historic win in Sunday's municipal elections in Berlin. We ask if the 45-year-old daughter of Turkish political exiles can push through her promises of rent freezes and nationalisation of private real estate companies. Just like in New York last year, affordable housing was a hot-button issue. It didn't hurt that her party ran a social media-savvy campaign.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>UK and US make first-ever torpedo test from uncrewed vessel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:978090d5b32fbececc8a1f4d4a02a66362b9c35cdbd04dd7952710ade37f67e4</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T02:33:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-uk-and-us-make-first-ever-torpedo-test-from-uncrewed-vessel--57411a117a8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-uk-and-us-make-first-ever-torpedo-test-from-uncrewed-vessel" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom and the United States have for the first time test-fired a torpedo from an uncrewed underwater vessel, the UK government said Monday, marking a step forward in AUKUS efforts to develop autonomous naval technology.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU to lift sanctions on Russian oligarchs Usmanov, Fridman</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8512bb54a474fefd837f669ae3e2c5689179c6a8e64b567de6e68c1fdd85f953</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T02:18:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-eu-fails-to-agree-on-lifting-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs--e6657fec7a6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-eu-fails-to-agree-on-lifting-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs" /><summary type="html">EU countries on Tuesday agreed a compromise deal to prolong sanctions on Russia that will see oligarchs Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman removed from the blacklist, diplomats said. Ukraine called the EU’s delisting of Usmanov and Fridman “shameful” and urged national sanctions.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Brigitte Bardot's personal possessions sell for nearly €1 million at Paris auction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2840eb998d71b0630421a80a4acd40990b5e7e4aa031e3873c4e836b4405bbc7</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T20:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bardot-auction-in-paris-fetches-nearly-one-million-euros--554822d4f57b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bardot-auction-in-paris-fetches-nearly-one-million-euros" /><summary type="html">An auction of the personal belongings of French screen icon Brigitte Bardot fetched nearly €1 million in Paris on Monday, with the sale featuring hundreds of personal objects ranging from sunglasses to furniture.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Bayeux Tapestry craze prompts photo ban at British Museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:053288005588aaca97364da314f47ac4a8c54cb213d442e40ed281b69c48ec54</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T15:45:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bayeux-tapestry-craze-prompts-photo-ban-at-british-museum--545565e72784.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bayeux-tapestry-craze-prompts-photo-ban-at-british-museum" /><summary type="html">The British Museum said on Monday that it has banned people from taking photos of the Bayeux Tapestry to prevent crowds from backing up at the new exhibit. The 1,000-year-old artwork is on display in the UK after an unprecedented loan from France, and tickets are sold out until December 31.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU fines Google €403 million for improperly using location data</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd6d77ebb976522a1a9e3aee4b6a0141fa0bb25a9b731df02686e013876f5e48</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T15:05:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-eu-fines-google-_403-million-for-improperly-using-location-data--76f449cd2c22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-eu-fines-google-%E2%82%AC403-million-for-improperly-using-location-data" /><summary type="html">Ireland, on behalf of the European Union, said Monday it had fined Google €403 million for improperly using users' location data between May 2018 and February 2020. However, the eight-year delay drew some criticism, as the European Consumer Organisation said that "can be as harmful as no enforcement at all".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz vows to hold ruling coalition together after election gains by far right, hard left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4462c7a9c2e28b098e4460ebb404e8bbdbb6ccbc12f85f4bcdba9ba285682fd2</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:02:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-germany-merz-vows-to-keep-ruling-coalition-together-after-election-defeats--662f6d074177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-germany-merz-vows-to-keep-ruling-coalition-together-after-election-defeats" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz vowed Monday to keep his ruling coalition of the centre-right CDU and centre-left SPD together for the sake of the country's "democratic future", after both the far right and hard left made big gains in Germany's state elections on Sunday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Five takeaways from Germany's regional elections after far-right gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db73d1707ee74a78eab0052544b1a98683a37c42cf8b193a6afc94016d80704a</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T06:47:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-five-takeaways-from-germany-s-regional-elections-after-far-right-gains--2b1574a8c4fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-five-takeaways-from-germany-s-regional-elections-after-far-right-gains" /><summary type="html">Sunday's elections in two German states resulted in the defeat of the country's ruling CDU, a result described as a “disaster” by Chancellor Friedrich Merz. In Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, in the northeast of the country, the far-right AfD became the strongest party while the hard-left Die Linke led the polls in Berlin.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
